      "widgets_values": [
        "Continuing exactly from the reference frame: the barn owl perches on the central weathered barn beam, white heart-shaped face, golden-speckled wings folded, lit by low morning light through plank gaps on the right. Within the first half-second it raises both wings and snaps them fully open into a wide, symmetrical display, then beats them in two powerful downstrokes while its talons keep gripping the beam, body staying centered above it. Spread primaries reveal pale undersides and fine dark barring; wingtips remain inside the central square. Dust swirls off the beam in the wing draft and spins through the light. The camera arcs smoothly left around the owl at constant distance, a blurred foreground post sliding across the frame edge and background beams shifting behind. Crisp feather detail, natural wildlife realism, one continuous shot.",
